quran[3]{c,v,t}:
  5,3,"Forbidden to you are carrion, blood, the flesh of swine, that animal on which the name of someone other than Allah is invoked at the time of slaughtering, and the animal that dies by strangling, and the animal beaten to death by a violent blow, and the animal which dies by falling, and the animal gored to death, and the animal which wild beasts have eaten, unless you still slaughter it (after it being wounded, in the correct manner), and the animal slaughtered on the stones set up for the idols and that you should allot shares (or decide fortunes) by the divining arrows—all of that is a transgression. Today, the disbelievers have lost all hope of (overcoming) your religion. Therefore, do not fear them but fear Me. Today, I have perfected your religion for you, completed My blessing upon you and approved Islam as your religion. But whoever is extremely compelled by hunger, without inclining purposely to sin, then Allah is indeed Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  5,4,"(O Prophet!) They ask you what is permissible for them (to eat). Say: ‘All good things are permissible for you. And as for what you have taught among the hunting dogs (to catch), teaching them out of what Allah has taught you, eat from what they have seized for you, but mention Allah’s Name over it, and be God-conscious. Indeed, Allah is swift at reckoning.’"
  5,5,"This day, all good things have been made permissible for you. The food of the People of the Book is made permissible for you, and your food is permissible for them. (Similarly,) the chaste from among the believing women and the chaste from among those given the Book before you (are permissible for you in marriage) when you have given them their bridal gifts, desiring chastity, not unlawful sexual intercourse or taking (them) as secret mistresses. And whoever renounces (his) faith, all his deeds will become void, and in the Hereafter, he will be among the losers."
